---
// Chapter 1: a sentence grows one word at a time, with real output from a small open model. Behaviour in src/scripts/demos.js.
---
<div class="panel demo" id="nw">
  <b>One word at a time</b>
  <p class="mono nw-line" id="nw-line" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="small nw-hint" id="nw-hint"></p>
  <div class="nw-opts" id="nw-opts"></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn pri" type="button" id="nw-auto">Let the model pick</button><button class="btn" type="button" id="nw-reset">Start over</button></div>
  <p class="small" id="nw-tally" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="caption">Real output from SmolLM2-360M, a small open model. The assistants you use are far larger and rarely get facts like these wrong. The mechanism is the same.</p>
</div>
